cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SelfHeal-AirTwin: a self-healing digital twin for drift detection and correction in low-cost urban air-quality sensors"
abstract: >-
  SelfHeal-AirTwin is a streaming digital twin for low-cost air-quality
  sensor networks. For every sensor it predicts the value the sensor should
  read from neighbouring sensors, weather and the reference analyzer, scores
  drift from the residual with EWMA and CUSUM, estimates an online offset and
  gain correction once drift is confirmed, publishes corrected values, and
  returns a ranked recalibration list to the physical network.
